    "id": "v2-da0e32-p9-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Priya has $\\$120$ and saves $\\$35$ each week. She wants to have at least $\\$500$ to buy a bike.\nWrite an inequality involving $w$, the number of weeks, and solve it. What can you say about the number of weeks?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$120+35w\\ge500$, so $w\\ge\\frac{76}{7}$. Priya needs to save for at least 11 weeks.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}120+35w&\\ge500\\\\35w&\\ge380\\\\w&\\ge\\frac{76}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac{76}{7}\\approx10.9$ and $w$ counts whole weeks, Priya needs to save for at least 11 weeks.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
